# TODO

- Prevent a timed-out Vitest fixture hook from racing the next case's database
  reset in the same worker. Vitest reports `hookTimeout` without cancelling the
  hook promise, and `deleteDrizzleRows` cannot discover arbitrary work started
  by suite-owned hooks. The existing detached-work drain covers only runtime
  work registered with that tracker. A safe fix therefore needs a worker-level
  fail-stop/cancellation contract from Vitest, or a mandatory hook-work tracker
  that every DB fixture awaits before reset. Do not add a delay, a longer
  timeout, or a reset-only mutex: each can release while the timed-out hook is
  still mutating the database and would only hide the race. See #616.
